1. Use the 'site:' search operator in Google search. This will return a number of results, which can give you an estimate of how many pages are indexed. Please note that this method may not be completely accurate.

2. Use Google Search Console. In the 'Coverage' report, you can see how many pages are 'Valid', which means they are in the Google index. Again, this is not a precise number, but it is a good estimate.

3. Use a third-party tool like SEMRush or Ahrefs. These tools have a feature that can show you an estimated number of indexed pages.

